lib/ also holds code that needs no notice here. fmt 12.1.0 is MIT with an exception for object
code. ThreadPool (https://github.com/progschj/ThreadPool) is zlib, which asks for its notice in
source copies only, and lib/ holds it as object code only. Cephes reaches MLX only through
fastermath and Julien Pommier's code, and its terms ask for no notice. MLX also cites papers,
documentation, math results and algorithms that it implements in code of its own, such as
Threefry, CUB's merge sort, VkFFT's Stockham FFT and Neil Sloane's table of Hadamard matrices.
